---
import Variant from '../../layouts/Variant.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<Variant
  title="ExCSV ZIP container"
  description="Ship one inner .excsv inside .excsv.zip with metadata summary in the ZIP archive comment."
  heading="ZIP container"
  lede="Compress a plain inline ExCSV file. Read schema and aggregations from the ZIP comment without extracting."
>
  <h2>Layout</h2>
  <pre><code>sales.excsv.zip
└── sales.excsv     ← primary entry (first in central directory)
    header + meta + data rows (inline plain form)</code></pre>

  <p>
    The inner file is a normal <a href="/variants/plain/">inline plain</a> document.
    Sidecar pairs are <strong>not</strong> zipped as a unit in v0.2 — use two plain files or materialize inline first.
  </p>

  <h2>Inner header</h2>
  <p>The inner <code>#!excsv</code> line <strong>MUST</strong> include <code>original-size=&lt;bytes&gt;</code>, matching the ZIP central directory <code>uncompressed_size</code>.</p>

  <CodeBlock title="ZIP comment (excerpt)" description="Advisory summary — inner file is authoritative.">
{`#!excsv version=0.2 delim=comma header=1 rows=4 original-size=18204 sql-dialect=postgres
#@source: sales_db.orders
#column name=id type=int
#column name=customer type=string
#$ddl: CREATE TABLE orders (...)
#%sum: ,,,1050.50
#@comment-truncated: 1`}
  </CodeBlock>

  <h2>Fast path</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open archive, locate primary entry (<code>sales.excsv</code> or <code>data.excsv</code>).</li>
    <li>Optionally parse the end-of-central-directory comment for metadata-only queries.</li>
    <li>Extract primary entry for full parse and checksum validation.</li>
  </ol>

  <p><a href="/spec/#zip-container">Normative §10</a> · <a href="/examples/">Zipped example</a></p>
</Variant>
